  "causalModel": {
   "founding": "The Xit-Xaht went on cutting stone after the Duskfall told every tribe to stop, on the order of a Hist they had bound with sap.",
   "siteAdvantages": "A firm rock shelf at the end of an upland ridge, 68 m by 42 m of buildable ground with the block face in its own southern lip, a headwater stream along that lip for mortar and slaking, and a 55 m escarpment on the east that no neighbour climbs uninvited.",
   "occupantsMotive": "Tsono-Xuhil has not woken. The Amber Plasm seep has resumed, the conduits carry it up the escarpment into the works, and the courses have started rising again.",
   "pressures": "Labour. Every course needs hands the tribe does not have, so the pens fill from the neighbouring villages; the shelf is also too small for what the shaper has drawn.",
   "wouldChangeIf": "The conduits were cut, or another tribe accepted the invitation to help."
  },
